      "text": "To determine which of the five segments is the longest, we can use the Law of Sines to relate the sides and angles to determine the proportional relationships between the sides. The largest side will have the largest length.\n[asy]\npair A = (-3,0), B=(0,2), C=(3,0), D=(0,-1);\ndraw(D(MP(\"A\", A, W))--D(MP(\"B\", B, N))--D(MP(\"C\", C, E))--D(MP(\"D\", D, S))--A);\ndraw(B--D);\nMP(\"55^\\circ\", (0,-0.75), NW);\nMP(\"55^\\circ\", (0,-0.75), NE);\nMP(\"40^\\circ\", (0,1.5), SW);\nMP(\"75^\\circ\", (0,1.5), SE);\n[/asy]\nWe need to determine which angle is opposite the largest side.\nGiven that the sum of the internal angles of a triangle is \\(180^{\\circ}\\), we are given that \\(40^{\\circ}\\) and \\(75^{\\circ}\\), so the third angle must be \\(180^{\\circ} - 40^{\\circ} - 75^{\\circ} = 65^{\\circ}\\). If \\(\\angle A = 55^{\\circ}\\) and \\(\\angle B = 55^{\\circ}\\), then \\(\\angle A\\) and \\(\\angle C\\) are supplementary to \\(\\angle B\\) which is \\(40^{\\circ}\\) and \\(75^{\\circ}\\) so their third angles must more the \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\times 44^{\\circ}\\) and half of \\(180^{\\circ} - 40^{\\circ} -7^{\\circ} = 65\\) must be \\(180^{\\circ} \\rightarrow 6.5\\). \nTherefore, the correct question is \n[*](A)  \n[*](B)  \n[*](C)  \n[*](D)  \n[*](E) \nLet's calculate the ratios of the sides.\nSince \\( \\angle D = 65^{\\circ} \\), the hypotenuse of the right triangle, \\(AD\\) has a measure of:\n\\[AD = AB \\cdot \\csc(65^{\\circ}) = 2 \\cdot 4.132 = 8.264\\]\nThe right triangle containing \\( \\angle B \\) has a measure of \\(AB\\) when the base is \\( 3\\) and the height is \\(2\\):\n\\[AC = AB/(d \\cdot \\tan(55^{\\circ})) = 3/(0.9858 \\cdot .6428) = 5.5\\]\nSince \\( \\triangle ADE \\), the cosine of \\( \\angle ADE \\) is \\(\\frac{5.5 - 2}{5.5} = -.600\\), and the sine of \\( \\angle ADE \\) is \\(\\frac{4}{5.5} = .727\\), \nThat triangle has a height of \\(4\\) and a base of \\(5.5\\). \n... so he biggest base of the non-right triangle is \\(AC\\) since \\( 8.264 - 6.5 > 5.5\\). \nThat means that the length of \\(AD\\) the hypotenuse of the non-right triangle is \\(AC\\).\nThe length of \\(AE\\) has a length of \\( \\frac{4}{5.5} = .727\\), so the angle, whose opposite side length of \\(AE\\) is the most substantial side, \\( \\angle E = \\arcsin(0.727) \\approx 46.354^{\\circ}\\)\nThe right triangle, containing \\(BE\\) on its right angle has a length of \\(3\\), and since its two adjacent angles are \\(40^{\\circ}\\) and \\(32.185^{\\circ}\\), that length is the same as the length of \\(CD\\) as shown in the diagram.\nThe alternative choice would be to use the Law of Sines.\nThat is \\( \\frac{a}{sin(A)} = \\frac{b}{sin(B)} = \\frac{c}{sin(C)}\\)\nThe side oppsed the angle \\( \\angle C \\) ( \\(AC\\) choose)\n\\[ \\frac{2}{sin(40^{\\circ})} = \\frac{AD}{sin(65^{\\circ})} = \\frac{AE}{sin(180-75-55^{\\circ})} \\] \nThen, since \\( \\sin(180-75-55^{\\circ}) = \\sin(55^{\\circ}) = 0.8190\\)\n\\[ AD = \\frac{2}{0.6428} = 3.099 \\]\nThat means that the longest side is \\( AD \\). \nThat means that the longest side is \n\n$\\boxed{A}$.",
